<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<WorkflowBuilder Version="2.9.0"
                 xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                 xmlns:ext="clr-namespace:;assembly=Extensions"
                 xmlns:rig="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Devices.Rigs;assembly=OpenRigs.Devices"
                 xmlns:task="clr-namespace:UclOpenCoenDomeNavigationTask;assembly=Extensions"
                 xmlns:core="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Core;assembly=OpenRigs.Core"
                 xmlns:zap="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Devices.Zapit;assembly=OpenRigs.Devices"
                 xmlns:orcl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Control;assembly=OpenRigs.Control"
                 xmlns:hd="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.HarpDevices;assembly=OpenRigs.HarpDevices"
                 xmlns:mf="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Manifest;assembly=OpenRigs.Manifest"
                 xmlns:lv="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.LiveView;assembly=OpenRigs.LiveView"
                 xmlns:orl="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Logging;assembly=OpenRigs.Logging"
                 xmlns:aud="clr-namespace:OpenRigs.Audio;assembly=OpenRigs.Audio"
                 xmlns:rx="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Reactive;assembly=Bonsai.Core"
                 xmlns:sys="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib"
                 xmlns:scr="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions;assembly=Bonsai.Scripting.Expressions"
                 xmlns:harp="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Harp;assembly=Bonsai.Harp"
                 xmlns:dsp="clr-namespace:Bonsai.Dsp;assembly=Bonsai.Dsp"
                 xmlns="https://bonsai-rx.org/2018/workflow">
  <Workflow>
    <Nodes>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="DisplayDevice" Description="The display the dome projector is on (ProjectorDisplay); a launch property." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>RigSetup</Name>
        <Description>Reads this machine's rig.yml (ReadLabRig, which publishes RigConfigDirectory and RigConfigs) into the lab rig model (open_rigs.rigs.lab_rig), opens every device with RigHardware (which starts the cameras 2 s after Start and reports Ready once the Harp clock is set, the spouts are homed and the mixer has started: ReadyWaitsFor) and opens the dome's display (ProjectorDisplay).</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:ReadLabRig.bonsai">
              <ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</ConfigRoot>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>SpoutStepSize</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="SpoutStepSize" />
              </PropertyMappings>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:RigHardware.bonsai">
              <Description>Every dome device, named as in the data, behind its subjects (Building Blocks): the Behavior board (wheel distance, pulses, the ZapitTrigger line cleared however the workflow stops), the timestamp generator (Timestamp, HarpClockSet), both Lickety Splits, the three cameras and the lick spout stage, which homes, goes in and handles the spout commands.</Description>
              <ReadyWaitsFor>HarpClockSet, SpoutsHomed, MixerStarted</ReadyWaitsFor>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>RigConfigs</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>ProjectionCalibration</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="DisplayDevice" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Vision:ProjectorDisplay.bonsai">
              <Description>The dome's BonVision window, mesh mapping and gamma correction from rig.yml's projectionCalibration; stimuli draw on DrawStimuli.</Description>
              <DisplayDevice>First</DisplayDevice>
              <WindowState>Fullscreen</WindowState>
              <Width>1920</Width>
              <Height>1080</Height>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source2" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
        <Property Name="SubjectId" Description="The mouse's lab ID; the launch's own, from rig-control." />
        <Property Name="SessionId" Description="The session number; the launch's own, from rig-control." />
        <Property Name="TaskPath" Description="The task file: rig-control's copy of the one chosen at launch, read at Start for the background noise and again at Go with the form's edits; from the editor, config\task-abstract-av-corridor.yml." />
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Initialization</Name>
        <Description>The experiment controller (OpenRigs.Control, ExperimentControl): SubjectId and SessionId from the launch, SpoutStepSize settable live (its subject's one default, shown to the controller by ParameterDefault a second after Start), ManualRewardDropUl, the 2.5 ul every RewardLeft and RewardRight gives before and during a run through the valve's calibration (Pip's fixed manual drop, 15 Nov 2026), the spout commands (handled by HarpLickSpoutStage in RigHardware) at any time; at Start TaskFilePath (TaskPath, the task file rig-control wrote at launch and writes again at Go with the form's edits), and at Go RunSettings (subject, session) and TrainingStage are published.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="Value" DisplayName="SubjectId" Description="The subject (mouse) lab ID." />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="StringProperty">
                <Value></Value>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>SubjectId</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="SessionId" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>SubjectId</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="SubjectId" />
              </PropertyMappings>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Control:ExperimentControl.bonsai">
              <SubjectId>UNMAPPED</SubjectId>
              <SessionId />
              <ControlEndpoint>@tcp://127.0.0.1:5561</ControlEndpoint>
              <Parameters>
                <Parameter>
                  <Name>TrainingStage</Name>
                  <Value>0</Value>
                  <Description>Row of the task file's trainingStages to run, 0 to 5 (Tom Childs' stages 1 to 6; a row past the end stops the workflow at Go): suggested from the mouse's earlier experiments of the modality.</Description>
                  <Minimum>0</Minimum>
                  <Maximum>5</Maximum>
                  <WholeNumber>true</WholeNumber>
                </Parameter>
                <Parameter>
                  <Name>SpoutStepSize</Name>
                  <Value />
                  <Description>Motor steps each spout nudge command moves, taken live while ready; until set, the SpoutStepSize subject's default (Initialization).</Description>
                  <Minimum>1</Minimum>
                  <WholeNumber>true</WholeNumber>
                </Parameter>
              </Parameters>
              <Commands>
                <Command>
                  <Name>RewardLeft</Name>
                  <Description>Give ManualRewardDropUl (2.5 ul) on the left spout, through its valve's calibration.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>RewardRight</Name>
                  <Description>Give ManualRewardDropUl (2.5 ul) on the right spout, through its valve's calibration.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>SpoutsHome</Name>
                  <Description>Move both spouts to the home position.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>SpoutsIn</Name>
                  <Description>Move both spouts to the in position.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>SpoutsOut</Name>
                  <Description>Move both spouts to the out position.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>SaveSpoutPositions</Name>
                  <Description>Save the spouts' in positions to this mouse's file.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>LeftUp</Name>
                  <Description>Nudge the left spout up by SpoutStepSize.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>LeftDown</Name>
                  <Description>Nudge the left spout down by SpoutStepSize.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>RightUp</Name>
                  <Description>Nudge the right spout up by SpoutStepSize.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>RightDown</Name>
                  <Description>Nudge the right spout down by SpoutStepSize.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>LeftFront</Name>
                  <Description>Nudge the left spout forward by SpoutStepSize.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>LeftBack</Name>
                  <Description>Nudge the left spout back by SpoutStepSize.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>RightFront</Name>
                  <Description>Nudge the right spout forward by SpoutStepSize.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>RightBack</Name>
                  <Description>Nudge the right spout back by SpoutStepSize.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>BaseLeft</Name>
                  <Description>Nudge the spout base left by SpoutStepSize.</Description>
                </Command>
                <Command>
                  <Name>BaseRight</Name>
                  <Description>Nudge the spout base right by SpoutStepSize.</Description>
                </Command>
              </Commands>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>SubjectId</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:SubscribeWhen" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>SubjectId</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>SessionId</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>RunSettingsValid</Name>
              <Description>Subject and session given.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>Item1.Trim().Length &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; Item2.Trim().Length &gt; 0</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:First" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>RunSettings</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="StringProperty">
                <Value>..\config\task-abstract-av-corridor.yml</Value>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>TaskFilePath</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="ExternalizedMapping">
              <Property Name="Value" DisplayName="TaskPath" Description="The task file: rig-control's copy of the one chosen at launch, read at Start for the background noise and again at Go with the form's edits; from the editor, config\task-abstract-av-corridor.yml." />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ParameterValue">
                <orcl:Name>TrainingStage</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>Convert.ToInt32(it)</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>TrainingStage</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrainingStage</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>trainingStage</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="IntProperty">
                <Value>150</Value>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject">
              <Name>SpoutStepSize</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnParameterSet">
                <orcl:Name>SpoutStepSize</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Name>StepSizeToInt</scr:Name>
              <scr:Expression>Convert.ToInt32(it)</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>SpoutStepSize</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="DoubleProperty">
                <Value>2.5</Value>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject">
              <Name>ManualRewardDropUl</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>SpoutStepSize</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:DelaySubscription">
                <rx:DueTime>PT1S</rx:DueTime>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ParameterDefault">
                <orcl:Name>SpoutStepSize</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="7" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="11" To="14" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="13" To="14" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="14" To="15" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="15" To="16" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="16" To="17" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="17" To="18" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="19" To="20" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="20" To="21" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="22" To="19" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="23" To="24" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="24" To="25" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="25" To="26" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="27" To="28" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="29" To="30" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="31" To="32" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="32" To="33" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="33" To="34" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="35" To="36" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="37" To="38" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="38" To="39" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="39" To="40" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Declarations</Name>
        <Description>Subjects several groups share: Zapit's replies (ConnectZapit declares its commands), reward requests (side, microlitres) for DeliverReward, and the task's events (TrialEvents), trial rows (TrialRow) and stimulus rows (StimulusRows).</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject" TypeArguments="zap:ZapitReply">
              <rx:Name>ZapitReplies</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject" TypeArguments="sys:Tuple(sys:String,sys:Double)">
              <rx:Name>RewardRequests</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject" TypeArguments="ext:CorridorEvent">
              <rx:Name>TrialEvents</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject" TypeArguments="harp:Timestamped(ext:TrialRow)">
              <rx:Name>TrialRow</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:PublishSubject" TypeArguments="harp:Timestamped(ext:StimulusStateRow)">
              <rx:Name>StimulusRows</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Task</Name>
        <Description>Reads the task file (TaskPath) at Start into LaunchTaskConfig, as rig-control wrote it at launch, for the background noise, which plays from Ready; at Go, with the form's edits, into TaskConfig, and checks it with the stage and rig.yml (CreateCorridorSetup: a stage past the table, a reward zone outside the sweep in src\waveforms\sweep.json, the optogenetics rules, the Zapit conditions file). Go stops the workflow if backgroundNoise was changed after launch, as the noise already plays at the launch's level. A real mouse on a rig without hardware triggering is the Zapit group's refusal.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskFilePath</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Item2</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="core:ReadTextFile" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="task:DeserializeFromYaml">
              <task:Type xsi:type="TypeMapping" TypeArguments="task:UclOpenCoenDomeNavigationTaskLogic" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskFilePath</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="core:ReadTextFile" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="task:DeserializeFromYaml">
              <task:Type xsi:type="TypeMapping" TypeArguments="task:UclOpenCoenDomeNavigationTaskLogic" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>LaunchTaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>LaunchTaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>BackgroundNoiseChanged?</Name>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>Item1.TaskParameters.BackgroundNoise.Enabled != Item2.TaskParameters.BackgroundNoise.Enabled || Item1.TaskParameters.BackgroundNoise.LevelDbfs != Item2.TaskParameters.BackgroundNoise.LevelDbfs</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="StringProperty">
                <Value>The background noise plays from Ready at the task file's backgroundNoise as launched, so it cannot be changed before Go: launch again to play it at another level.</Value>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="core:ThrowError" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrainingStage</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>RigConfigs</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:CreateCorridorSetup">
                <ext:SweepFile>waveforms\sweep.json</ext:SweepFile>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>CorridorSetup</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>TaskParameters.Optogenetics.UseZapit</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>Optogenetics</Name>
              <Description>Whether this is an optogenetics experiment, from the task file (TaskParameters.Optogenetics.UseZapit): ExperimentManifest requires Zapit&apos;s logs only while it is true (ExpectedFiles ?Optogenetics).</Description>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="12" To="14" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="13" To="14" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="14" To="15" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="15" To="16" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="16" To="17" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="18" To="21" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="19" To="21" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="20" To="21" Label="Source3" />
            <Edge From="21" To="22" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="22" To="23" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="24" To="25" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="25" To="26" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Zapit</Name>
        <Description>Zapit, only in an optogenetics experiment: OpenRigs.Devices Zapit.ConnectZapit, given the task's conditions file, connects to rig.yml's Zapit, carries ZapitCommands and ZapitReplies, and stops the workflow on an error reply, no conditions file loaded, a conditions count other than the file's, or a real mouse on a rig without hardware triggering.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>OptogeneticsExperiment?</Name>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>TaskParameters.Optogenetics.UseZapit</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>TaskParameters.Optogenetics.ZapitConfigPath</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:Zapit.ConnectZapit.bonsai" />
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Commands</Name>
        <Description>RewardLeft and RewardRight give ManualRewardDropUl (2.5 ul, Initialization) on that side (DeliverReward). The spout commands are RigHardware's (HarpLickSpoutStage).</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnCommand">
                <orcl:Name>RewardLeft</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="StringProperty">
                <Value>left</Value>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ManualRewardDropUl</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:WithLatestFrom" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>RewardRequests</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:OnCommand">
                <orcl:Name>RewardRight</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="StringProperty">
                <Value>right</Value>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ManualRewardDropUl</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:WithLatestFrom" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>RewardRequests</Name>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="0" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source2" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Grating</Name>
        <Description>The grating (BonVision DrawGratings) on the dome: each pip sets its spatial frequency and opacity (TaskLogic); off between trials.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>DrawStimuli</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="sys:Double">
              <rx:Name>GratingSpatialFrequency</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="SpatialFrequency" Selector="it" />
              </PropertyMappings>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:BehaviorSubject" TypeArguments="sys:Double">
              <rx:Name>GratingOpacity</rx:Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="Opacity" />
              </PropertyMappings>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="BonVision:Primitives.DrawGratings.bonsai">
              <LocationX>0</LocationX>
              <LocationY>30</LocationY>
              <Layer>1</Layer>
              <ExtentX>270</ExtentX>
              <ExtentY>105</ExtentY>
              <SpatialFrequency>0.3</SpatialFrequency>
              <TemporalFrequency>0</TemporalFrequency>
              <Phase>16.8036766</Phase>
              <Angle>90</Angle>
              <SquareWave>false</SquareWave>
              <Contrast>1</Contrast>
              <DutyCycle xsi:nil="true" />
              <Radius>1000</Radius>
              <Aperture>0</Aperture>
              <Opacity>0</Opacity>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="2" To="5" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source3" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Audio</Name>
        <Description>The dome speakers and their mixer (OpenRigs.Audio SpeakerMixer: Speakers, rig.yml's speakers and filters loaded once at Start, and the mixer started no sooner than 3 s after Start, as a fault while the sound card boots can blue-screen the PC). At Go, each sound is laid out at the task file's level in dBFS RMS (levelDbfs), which stops the workflow if any would peak at -1 dBFS after equalisation: the pips (PipBuffers, tonePips.levelDbfs) and the reward tone (RewardTone, rewardTone.levelDbfs) on every rig.yml speaker, each equalised with its filter; the lab's penalty sound (PenaltySoundBuffer) on rig.yml's penaltySoundChannel alone at penalty.sound.levelDbfs. The background noise is on every speaker as it is, at the launch's task file's backgroundNoise.levelDbfs (LaunchTaskConfig), laid out at Start and sent to the mixer at Ready, which loops it and fades it in over 2 s. TaskLogic sends the pips, the reward tone and the penalty sound to the mixer (StimulusSounds, RewardToneSounds, PenaltySounds), which plays them over each other.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Audio:SpeakerMixer.bonsai" />
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>TaskParameters.TonePips.LevelDbfs</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Speakers</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dsp:MatrixReader">
                <dsp:Path>./waveforms/all_waveforms.bin</dsp:Path>
                <dsp:Offset>0</dsp:Offset>
                <dsp:SampleRate>48000</dsp:SampleRate>
                <dsp:ChannelCount>1</dsp:ChannelCount>
                <dsp:BufferLength>2400</dsp:BufferLength>
                <dsp:Depth>F32</dsp:Depth>
                <dsp:Layout>RowMajor</dsp:Layout>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:ToList" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="InputMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="LevelDbfs" Selector="Item1" />
              </PropertyMappings>
              <Selector>Item2</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="aud:SpeakerBuffer">
                <aud:LevelDbfs>-30</aud:LevelDbfs>
                <aud:Equalise>true</aud:Equalise>
                <aud:SyncCopy>true</aud:SyncCopy>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>PipBuffers</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>TaskParameters.RewardTone.LevelDbfs</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Speakers</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dsp:MatrixReader">
                <dsp:Path>./waveforms/reward_tone.bin</dsp:Path>
                <dsp:Offset>0</dsp:Offset>
                <dsp:SampleRate>0</dsp:SampleRate>
                <dsp:ChannelCount>1</dsp:ChannelCount>
                <dsp:BufferLength>0</dsp:BufferLength>
                <dsp:Depth>F32</dsp:Depth>
                <dsp:Layout>RowMajor</dsp:Layout>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="InputMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="LevelDbfs" Selector="Item1" />
              </PropertyMappings>
              <Selector>Item2</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="aud:SpeakerBuffer">
                <aud:LevelDbfs>-36</aud:LevelDbfs>
                <aud:Equalise>true</aud:Equalise>
                <aud:SyncCopy>false</aud:SyncCopy>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>RewardTone</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>TaskParameters.Penalty.Sound.LevelDbfs</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Speakers</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="InputMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="LevelDbfs" Selector="Item1" />
              </PropertyMappings>
              <Selector>Item2</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="aud:PenaltySoundBuffer">
                <aud:LevelDbfs>-30</aud:LevelDbfs>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>PenaltySoundBuffer</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>LaunchTaskConfig</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>BackgroundNoiseEnabled?</Name>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>TaskParameters.BackgroundNoise.Enabled</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>TaskParameters.BackgroundNoise.LevelDbfs</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Speakers</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="dsp:MatrixReader">
                <dsp:Path>./waveforms/background_noise.bin</dsp:Path>
                <dsp:Offset>0</dsp:Offset>
                <dsp:SampleRate>0</dsp:SampleRate>
                <dsp:ChannelCount>1</dsp:ChannelCount>
                <dsp:BufferLength>0</dsp:BufferLength>
                <dsp:Depth>F32</dsp:Depth>
                <dsp:Layout>RowMajor</dsp:Layout>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="InputMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="LevelDbfs" Selector="Item1" />
              </PropertyMappings>
              <Selector>Item2</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="aud:SpeakerBuffer">
                <aud:LevelDbfs>-50</aud:LevelDbfs>
                <aud:Equalise>false</aud:Equalise>
                <aud:SyncCopy>false</aud:SyncCopy>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>BackgroundNoise</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
              <Name>Ready</Name>
              <Description>Passes on once every stage RigHardware's ReadyWaitsFor names has come, the moment RigHardware reports Ready: HarpClockSet, the spouts homed (LickSpoutStage.Homed) and the mixer started (MixerStarted, SpeakerMixer's one stage on ReadyStages), so the background noise starts at Ready.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>HarpClockSet</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                      <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>LickSpoutStage.Homed</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                      <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>ReadyStages</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                      <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="6" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source3" />
                  <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Item1</Selector>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="3" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="2" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="14" To="15" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="13" To="16" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="15" To="16" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="12" To="17" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="16" To="17" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="17" To="18" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="18" To="19" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="19" To="20" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="21" To="22" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="22" To="24" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="23" To="24" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="24" To="25" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="25" To="26" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="26" To="27" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="28" To="29" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="29" To="30" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="32" To="33" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="31" To="34" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="33" To="34" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="30" To="35" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="34" To="35" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="35" To="36" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="36" To="37" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="37" To="40" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="39" To="40" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="40" To="41" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="41" To="38" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>StartTrials</Name>
        <Description>Trials start 0.5 s after the experiment folder exists and the tones are loaded (TrialsReady).</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>CorridorSetup</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>PathPrefix</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>PipBuffers</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Zip" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Item1</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Delay">
                <rx:DueTime>PT0.5S</rx:DueTime>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:AsyncSubject">
              <Name>TrialsReady</Name>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="3" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source3" />
            <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>TaskLogic</Name>
        <Description>The task in tested C# (src\Extensions\Corridor.cs, tests\Extensions.Tests): CorridorTask draws each trial (TrialDraw) at the start of its interval (the last outcome after any timeout), has a hardware-triggered Zapit armed during it (Arm, once the last trigger line has fallen), starts it at Go (Start, beep 0: the interval's end less the lead, max(laserToStimulusSeconds, 0), or later until the stage's quiet waits hold), then runs it along the virtual track (VirtualTrack) with a pip every 50 ms from the lead after Go, all on the Harp clock (Timestamp), until the outcome. Its events drive the hardware here: Arm sends Zapit the trial's condition (laser-off trials at 0 mW); Trigger, laserToStimulusSeconds before the first pip (after it if negative), raises the ZapitTrigger line (and on a software-triggered rig sends the StartStimulus) in an optogenetics experiment only, and CorridorTask stops the task if Zapit has not answered by then; Pip plays the pip and sets the grating; Outcome writes the trial row, rewards (DeliverReward, left spout) or plays the penalty sound, and in an optogenetics experiment clears the trigger line triggerHoldSeconds later (HarpDelay). Zapit adds no time.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialsReady</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Timestamp</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>WheelDistanceCm</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>LickStateLeft</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ZapitReplies</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:CorridorTask" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:CorridorEvents">
                <ext:Kind>Arm</ext:Kind>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:ZapitTrialCommand">
                <ext:HardwareTriggered>true</ext:HardwareTriggered>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>ZapitCommands</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:CorridorEvents">
                <ext:Kind>Start</ext:Kind>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Trial.trialNumber</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>trialNumber</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Trial.rewardSizeUl</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>rewardSizeUl</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Trial.laserCondition</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>laserCondition</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>Optogenetics?</Name>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>Trial.optogenetics</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ZapitTriggerLine</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:WithLatestFrom" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Item2</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="zap:ZapitLineMessage">
                <zap:Set>true</zap:Set>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>SoftwareTriggered?</Name>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>Trial.optogenetics &amp;&amp; !Trial.armZapit</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:ZapitTrialCommand">
                <ext:HardwareTriggered>false</ext:HardwareTriggered>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>ZapitCommands</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
              <Name>LaserOnUntilOutcome</Name>
              <Description>From the trigger, stops Zapit once per optogenetics trial: at the outcome, at laserMaxSeconds on the Harp clock (LaserCap), or at laserMaxSeconds on the wall clock, a backstop should the board stall (the one wall-clock wait in TaskLogic). A trial that ends before its trigger has no laser; the next StartStimulus disarms it.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="ext:CorridorEvents">
                      <ext:Kind>Outcome</ext:Kind>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="ext:CorridorEvents">
                      <ext:Kind>LaserCap</ext:Kind>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Name>LaserMax</scr:Name>
                    <scr:Expression>TimeSpan.FromSeconds(Trial.laserMaxSeconds)</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="DueTime" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Timer">
                      <rx:DueTime>PT12.5S</rx:DueTime>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Merge" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                      <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="ext:StopZapit" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
                    <Name>ZapitCommands</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                  <Expression xsi:type="Unit" />
                  <Expression xsi:type="Unit" />
                  <Expression xsi:type="Unit" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="0" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="13" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="14" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="7" To="15" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="13" To="8" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="14" To="8" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="15" To="8" Label="Source3" />
                  <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:CorridorEvents">
                <ext:Kind>Pip</ext:Kind>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>PipBuffers</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:WithLatestFrom" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:PipBuffer" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>StimulusSounds</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Frame.Row.visualSpatialFrequencyCpd</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>GratingSpatialFrequency</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Frame.GratingOpacity</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>GratingOpacity</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:CreateStimulusRow" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>StimulusRows</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:CorridorEvents">
                <ext:Kind>Outcome</ext:Kind>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="DoubleProperty">
                <Value>0</Value>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>GratingOpacity</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:CreateTrialRow" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>TrialRow</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>Rewarded?</Name>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>Rewarded</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Reward</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>RewardRequests</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>RewardTone</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:WithLatestFrom" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Item2</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>RewardToneSounds</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>PenaltySound?</Name>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>PenaltySound</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>PenaltySoundBuffer</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:WithLatestFrom" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Item2</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>PenaltySounds</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:Condition">
              <Name>OptogeneticsOutcome?</Name>
              <Description>Only an optogenetics experiment clears the trigger line, as only one raises it (Pip, 13 Nov 2026).</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowInput">
                    <Name>Source1</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
                    <scr:Expression>Trial.optogenetics</scr:Expression>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="2" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="InputMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="DueSeconds" Selector="Trial.triggerHoldSeconds" />
              </PropertyMappings>
              <Selector>it</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>Timestamp</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="core:HarpDelay">
                <core:DueSeconds>1</core:DueSeconds>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ZapitTriggerLine</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:WithLatestFrom" />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Selector>Item2</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="zap:ZapitLineMessage">
                <zap:Set>false</zap:Set>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>BehaviorBoard-Main.Commands</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:CorridorEvents">
                <ext:Kind>Trigger</ext:Kind>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>TrialEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="ext:CorridorEvents">
                <ext:Kind>Start</ext:Kind>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
              <Name>RngSeed</Name>
              <Description>The seed every draw of the experiment follows from (the task file's rngSeed, or one drawn at Go when it is null), logged once at trial 1's Go: the Take(1) is after the multicast, so the shared AsyncEvents subject never completes.</Description>
              <Selector>Trial.rngSeed</Selector>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orl:CreateAsyncEvent">
                <orl:Event>RngSeed</orl:Event>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="Bonsai.Harp:WithLatestTimestamp.bonsai">
              <Name>Timestamp</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>AsyncEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="rx:Take">
                <rx:Count>1</rx:Count>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="0" To="5" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="1" To="5" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="2" To="5" Label="Source3" />
            <Edge From="3" To="5" Label="Source4" />
            <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source5" />
            <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="12" To="13" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="13" To="14" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="12" To="15" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="15" To="16" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="12" To="17" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="17" To="18" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="69" To="19" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="19" To="21" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="20" To="21" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="21" To="22" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="22" To="23" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="23" To="24" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="69" To="25" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="25" To="26" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="26" To="27" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="19" To="28" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="29" To="30" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="30" To="32" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="31" To="32" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="32" To="33" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="33" To="34" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="30" To="35" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="35" To="36" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="30" To="37" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="37" To="38" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="30" To="39" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="39" To="40" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="41" To="42" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="42" To="43" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="43" To="44" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="42" To="45" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="45" To="46" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="42" To="47" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="47" To="48" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="48" To="49" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="47" To="51" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="50" To="51" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="51" To="52" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="52" To="53" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="42" To="54" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="54" To="56" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="55" To="56" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="56" To="57" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="57" To="58" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="42" To="59" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="59" To="60" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="60" To="62" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="61" To="62" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="62" To="64" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="63" To="64" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="64" To="65" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="65" To="66" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="66" To="67" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="68" To="69" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="70" To="71" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="71" To="72" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="72" To="73" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="73" To="74" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="74" To="75" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="75" To="76" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
        <Name>Logging</Name>
        <Description>Everything written to the experiment folder: LogControllerLogic makes the folder at Go and publishes PathPrefix; ExperimentLogs holds every log that waits for it; HarpLogs records the Harp boards; DeliverReward delivers and logs rewards; BonsaiData_Async takes the controller's events; RecordHarpDevices, ExperimentManifest and the Recording phase follow PathPrefix.</Description>
        <Workflow>
          <Nodes>
            <Expression xsi:type="GroupWorkflow">
              <Name>LogControllerLogic</Name>
              <Description>Waits for Go (RunSettings: the controller's SubjectId and SessionId), then LogController creates the experiment folder RootPath\sub-&lt;SubjectId&gt;\ses-&lt;SessionId&gt;_&lt;DateTime&gt; and publishes it as PathPrefix, which every log waits for. RootPath is rig.yml's, the rig's acquisition folder itself (C:\Coen-Lab-Local\Acquired-Data): experiments have no project folder.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>RunSettings</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="SubjectId" Selector="Item1" />
                      <Property Name="SessionId" Selector="Item2" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>RigConfigs</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="MemberSelector">
                    <Selector>RootPath</Selector>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
                    <PropertyMappings>
                      <Property Name="Path" />
                    </PropertyMappings>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogController.bonsai">
                    <SubjectId>UNMAPPED</SubjectId>
                    <SessionId>UNMAPPED</SessionId>
                    <Path>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\Acquired-Data</Path>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:DelaySubscription">
                      <rx:DueTime>PT1S</rx:DueTime>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>RunSettings</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rx:SubscribeWhen" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="WorkflowOutput" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="3" To="4" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="1" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="6" To="8" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source2" />
                  <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogAsync.bonsai">
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>PathPrefix</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="rx:SelectMany">
              <Name>ExperimentLogs</Name>
              <Description>Starts every experiment log once LogControllerLogic publishes PathPrefix: BonsaiData_Trial (LogTrial; one row per trial, built by CreateTrialRow when the outcome is known; columns in schemas\trial-columns.yml), BonsaiData_StimulusState (one row per pip), the cameras (OpenRigs.Logging LogCameras), the settings files (Settings_Rig, Settings_Task, Settings_Experiment) and Zapit's logs (OpenRigs.Devices Zapit.ZapitLogs: its replies, and Settings_ZapitConditions in an optogenetics experiment). The RngSeed event is TaskLogic's, at trial 1's Go.</Description>
              <Workflow>
                <Nodes>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>TrialRow</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogTrial.bonsai">
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>StimulusRows</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogData.bonsai">
                    <LogName>BonsaiData_StimulusState</LogName>
                    <Selector />
                    <AutoFlush>true</AutoFlush>
                    <Extension>csv</Extension>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>RigConfigs</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="rig:SerializeToJson">
                      <rig:Formatting>Indented</rig:Formatting>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogDataSchema.bonsai">
                    <Name>Settings_Rig</Name>
                    <Extension>json</Extension>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>TaskConfig</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="task:SerializeToJson">
                      <task:Formatting>Indented</task:Formatting>
                    </Combinator>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogDataSchema.bonsai">
                    <Name>Settings_Task</Name>
                    <Extension>json</Extension>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
                    <Name>ExperimentGo</Name>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
                    <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ExperimentSettings" />
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogDataSchema.bonsai">
                    <Name>Settings_Experiment</Name>
                    <Extension>json</Extension>
                  </Expression>
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Logging:LogCameras.bonsai" />
                  <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:Zapit.ZapitLogs.bonsai" />
                </Nodes>
                <Edges>
                  <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="4" To="5" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="5" To="6" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="8" To="9" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
                  <Edge From="11" To="12" Label="Source1" />
                </Edges>
              </Workflow>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:HarpLogs.bonsai">
              <Description>One LogHarpDevice per dome Harp device, from the experiment folder and the Harp clock being set.</Description>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>RewardRequests</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>RigFile</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="PropertyMapping">
              <PropertyMappings>
                <Property Name="RigFile" />
              </PropertyMappings>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="OpenRigs.Devices:BehaviorBoard.DeliverReward.bonsai">
              <Description>Each reward (side, microlitres), planned from that side's valve calibration and fired on the Harp clock at the calibration's pulseGapMs; a RewardDelivered row in BonsaiData_Async and each calibrated valve's file as ValveCalibrationDO&lt;n&gt;.</Description>
              <RigFile>UNMAPPED</RigFile>
              <CalibrationDirectory />
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>PathPrefix</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportMetric">
                <orcl:Name>path</orcl:Name>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orcl:ReportPhase">
                <orcl:Phase>Recording</orcl:Phase>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="hd:RecordHarpDevices">
              <Name>RecordHarpDevices</Name>
              <Description>Checks every Harp device in rig.yml at Start and records it into each experiment (OpenRigs.HarpDevices): the Behavior board, the timestamp generator, both stepper drivers and both Lickety Splits (each a rig.yml entry with a portName whose data the workflow publishes as &lt;Name&gt;.Data) must be on their portName with their usbSerial, or the workflow stops saying which board is where; 0.5 s after the experiment folder appears it asks each for a register dump on &lt;Name&gt;.Commands, which its log records; and it writes &lt;Name&gt;\&lt;Name&gt;_device.json and the register map &lt;Name&gt;\&lt;Name&gt;.yml, which ExperimentManifest expects (harp).</Description>
              <hd:ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</hd:ConfigRoot>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="mf:ExperimentManifest">
              <Name>ExperimentManifest</Name>
              <Description>Writes manifest.json into the experiment folder (OpenRigs.Manifest), as av-dome's: the machine, this repo's commit, who launched it and sent Go, rig.yml and the calibration files the workflow reads (MeshMap.csv, gammalut.bmp, the three speakers' filters, this mouse's spout positions) by hash, what each BonsaiData_Trial column means (schemas\trial-columns.yml), and what the experiment must leave: a folder for each device in rig.yml, the Harp device records, the three settings files and BonsaiData (Trial, Async and StimulusState); DeliverReward copies each calibrated valve's file in as ValveCalibrationDO&lt;n&gt;.</Description>
              <mf:IngestScript>coen-dome-navigation</mf:IngestScript>
              <mf:ConfigFiles>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs\%COMPUTERNAME%\rig.yml;C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs\%COMPUTERNAME%\calibration\MeshMap.csv;C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs\%COMPUTERNAME%\calibration\gammalut.bmp;C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs\%COMPUTERNAME%\calibration\speaker-left.json;C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs\%COMPUTERNAME%\calibration\speaker-right.json;C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs\%COMPUTERNAME%\calibration\speaker-centre.json;C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs\%COMPUTERNAME%\calibration\LickSpoutPositions\{SubjectId}.csv</mf:ConfigFiles>
              <mf:ExpectedFiles>auto;harp;Settings/Settings_Rig_;Settings/Settings_Task_;Settings/Settings_Experiment_;BonsaiData/BonsaiData_Trial_;BonsaiData/BonsaiData_Async_;BonsaiData/BonsaiData_StimulusState_;BonsaiData/BonsaiData_ZapitReplies_?Optogenetics;Settings/Settings_ZapitConditions_?Optogenetics</mf:ExpectedFiles>
              <mf:TrialColumns>schemas\trial-columns.yml</mf:TrialColumns>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="SubscribeSubject">
              <Name>ControlEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="scr:ExpressionTransform">
              <scr:Expression>new((it.Kind.ToString() == &quot;Command&quot; ? it.Name : it.Kind.ToString()) as Event, it.ToString() as Detail)</scr:Expression>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="Combinator">
              <Combinator xsi:type="orl:CreateAsyncEvent">
                <orl:Event>Control</orl:Event>
              </Combinator>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="IncludeWorkflow" Path="Bonsai.Harp:WithLatestTimestamp.bonsai">
              <Name>Timestamp</Name>
            </Expression>
            <Expression xsi:type="MulticastSubject">
              <Name>AsyncEvents</Name>
            </Expression>
          </Nodes>
          <Edges>
            <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="6" To="7" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="5" To="8" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="7" To="8" Label="Source2" />
            <Edge From="9" To="10" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="10" To="11" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="14" To="15" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="15" To="16" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="16" To="17" Label="Source1" />
            <Edge From="17" To="18" Label="Source1" />
          </Edges>
        </Workflow>
      </Expression>
      <Expression xsi:type="lv:StreamDevices">
        <Name>LiveView</Name>
        <Description>Streams every device in this machine's rig.yml that the workflow publishes, over ZeroMQ, for the live view (OpenRigs.LiveView): data on TCP 5556, video on 5558, from Start, in ready mode too. The three cameras as Camera-Face/Pupil/Body.video, 5 JPEG frames a second at 320 x 240, and the Behavior board's encoder from BehaviorBoard-Main.Data, 10 a second; each rate and size can be changed in rig.yml under the device's liveView:. Also elapsed, seconds since the experiment folder appeared, and liveview, this workflow and its commit. Every message carries the rig and the session key, ready until the experiment folder exists. Last in the workflow, because it streams only subjects built before it. A port already in use stops the workflow at Start.</Description>
        <lv:ConfigRoot>C:\Coen-Lab-Local\RigConfigs</lv:ConfigRoot>
        <lv:DataPort>5556</lv:DataPort>
        <lv:VideoPort>5558</lv:VideoPort>
      </Expression>
    </Nodes>
    <Edges>
      <Edge From="0" To="1" Label="Source1" />
      <Edge From="2" To="3" Label="Source1" />
    </Edges>
  </Workflow>
</WorkflowBuilder>
